      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2025-07-17T00:21:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-17T00:21:25Z",
    "body": "As I caught in #1500, nope, I misunderstood the LL(1) restrictions. `async sequence` still violates LL(1), because it shares a prefix with `async iterable`. The only way around that would be to form the two words into a single token, but that fixes a particular whitespace, so isn't really doable.\n\nSo no, I think `async_sequence<>` is the way to go. I'm actually more okay keeping `async iterable` and `async_sequence` differing in space vs underscore, but I can go change #1500 to use underscore in both places if desired.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
