    "created_at": "2025-07-18T18:57:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-18T18:57:18Z",
    "body": "This isn't about the number types, fwiw. `async iterable<>` is the declaration that makes *an interface* into an async iterable, like `iterable`. The number types are instead alongside `async_sequence<>`, which uses the underscore in contravention of the (current) precedent the number types set.\n\nBut I'm happy to have them both use underscores, it just means we'll need to modify a few specs that currently  use `async iterable`.",
